      "description": "Photograph collection ca. 1860s-1960s.\n(Note from seefooddiet: I tried to nail down a date for when Ogawa was in Korea through Korean and Japanese-language research, but had a hard time. His en/kowiki articles say he was in Korea in 1886, but they're unsourced. I suspect this pic is either late 1880s or early 1890s; very few Japanese people were in Seoul by 1885 (see this link for stats). I saw that he had a branch office for his company in Seoul by the 1890s, and he published photographs of the Sino-Japanese War in 1894. So \"at earliest late 1880s\" is the best I can do.)",
